{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XuX6neKFPTpNtAfs5eN5GV","type":"tool_result","content":"=== scripting-next-next-finish\n10:VARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509). Same 5-set bundle shape (outer zip holding evidence-01..05.zip) as the GM-verified auto-mastery cases; the solver answered 3075/3075 but the attempt EXPIRED (submit RemoteDisconnected after 5.42 s solve on Homebase). expected.json = solver output, spot-checked against the raw bytes (PS base64 record, VBS Codec_ field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n11-\n12:## Proposed lib additions\n13-- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n14-  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n15-  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n16-- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n=== binary-bridge-troll\n13:## Proposed lib additions\n14-- `lib.common.fast_aes_unzip(data, passwords)` -> [(name, Future[bytes])] + sha256 cache: the `_aes_member` / `_fast_unzip` pair in day09 binary-nimble solve.py (WinZip AE-x without pyzipper's pure-Python HMAC pass; zlib/pycryptodome/hashlib release the GIL so members inflate in parallel). Every lane whose evidence.zip carries a large member benefits.\n15-VARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no answer change) the \"8.21s on single_solve\" flag was CPU contention from parallel solver-tests, not the solver: isolated it runs 0.55-0.60 s wall on the single (taskset 2 vCPUs, ~0.75 s CPU) and 1.2 s on a 3-set Mastery; critical path is the d08 67 MB Swift member's AES-CTR||inflate||sha256 pipeline (done at ~0.37 s) + ~0.09 s of field analysis -- measure with `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`, not under a loaded solver-test.\n16-\n17-VARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D14) the \"4.11 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.51 s wall (0.6 s unpinned; the harness cProfile itself shows 0.048 s for import), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-7439276e 1.42 s wall pinned / 0.80 s unpinned; all 21 cases pass with every answer_id filled. Nothing to trim that the earlier cycles have not already trimmed.\n18-\n19-VARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D15) the \"4.84 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6.6, harness cProfile counted 1.1 s of imports and 2.9 s of thread waits) -- isolated and pinned to 2 CPUs: single 0.90 s wall (critical path = AES-CTR+inflate of the 67 MB d08 member ~0.2 s, HCFG scans 0.09 s, capstone import 0.07 s), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-546ae191 2.6 s pinned / 1.4 s unpinned; all 23 cases pass with every answer_id filled (solver-test single 1.26 s under concurrent load).\n20-\n21-## D17 (decoder-ring) single\n--\n29:## Proposed lib additions\n30-- lib/vocab.json: storage / hcfg_storage = \"base64\" for a base64 (SENGR...) stored HCFG (GM D17 d09/d08/d11/d13); \"raw\" REJECTED for raw-stored (D17 d12/d14).\n31-\n32-VARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D17) the \"3.31 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5; harness cProfile counted ~1.1 s of imports and ~2.4 s of thread waits) -- isolated: solve.py 0.8-0.9 s wall on the 204-id single (run_solver 0.87 s; tottime is 0.24 s threaded zlib inflate of the AES members + ~0.2 s imports), 1.1 s inside the full concurrent solver-test; all 31 cases green. `hctf solver-run` wall (~6.5 s) is CLI/harness startup under load, not the solver. d12/d14 `hcfg_storage` (raw-stored) stay intentionally empty (unresolved GM label), so the single outputs 202/204.\n33-\n34-VARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D20) the \"5.28 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~10; the harness cProfile of the same case totals 2.2 s, mostly thread waits + imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.61 s wall unpinned, 0.61-0.74 s pinned to 1-2 CPUs on the 240-id single; in-process answer() work is 0.28 s CPU once members are decoded, unzip 0.55 s CPU (67 MB d08 inflate ~0.16 s, pycryptodome AES-CTR 25 MB ~0.1 s, sha256 ~0.04 s, all GIL-free threads); full suite passes, Mastery 0.6-2.6 s. d20_analysis_hcfg_resource_size = RS20 u32le @ magic+8 (380 on the single, matches expected).\n35-\n36-VARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D21) the \"4.46 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~7-12; harness cProfile of the same case totals 1.83 s, mostly thread waits on the AES/inflate pool + 0.39 s imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.60-0.70 s wall unpinned, 0.93-1.1 s pinned to 2 CPUs on the 252-id single (252/252 match expected); no hot spot in tottime (threaded zlib inflate 0.26 s, hcfg scans 0.1 s, AES-CTR 0.09 s). Full suite 45/45 green, slowest 5-set Mastery 2.3 s inside the loaded concurrent solver-test. Nothing new to trim; the d21 loader/plugin (.cmxs) analysis adds no measurable cost.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Solver for this challenge -- harness skeleton. Fill in `answer()`; keep the I/O contract unchanged.\n\n    solve.py --contract <contract.json> --artifacts <dir>   ->  prints {answer_id: value} as JSON on the last line\n\nRuns on the Homebase VM inside a ~6-7 s window for EVERY Mastery set: stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/\n