{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHLpLm4oR9nTiwuuNGMz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The day22 ratchet gate is green (`python3 -m hctf.orchestrate ratchet-gate day22` exits 0 after the final edit).\n\n1. **Web (both proposals merged, both GM-CORRECT on single, TT and Mastery):** the `csrf` and `upload` handlers from the two solvers are now in `lib/web/handlers` and registered in `_KEY_MAP`. `for_key` now checks every clue key, not just the dispatch key, because the class name was in a sibling key both times (the dispatch keys were `current_user` and `preview_guide`). `lib.web.solve_target` now accepts already-fetched clues and returns None right away for an expired target (clues name no route and the home page isn't 2xx/3xx). The GM facts are in `lib/knowledge.py` (`WEB_CSRF_*`, `WEB_UPLOAD_*`).\n2. **Web bug found while merging:** `lib.web.solve()` passed a local function to the fork process pool, which can't serialise it. So any contract with 2+ targets came back `{}`. `solve()` and `main()` now both use a module-level `_run_target`, and targets run in parallel.\n3. **Warmups:** the D22 codec wasn't in `lib/warmups_codecs.py DAYS`. I added it as `(22, \"b64-zlib\")`: base64 of zlib, level 9, Z_FILTERED. It reproduces the single and TT blobs byte for byte and all 108 Mastery line-22 entries. `decode_chunked` now gets all 108 Mastery slugs right.\n4. **Metadata:** the prebuilt `jar.jar_manifest` gave the confirmed `jar.main_class` value (\"arena.evidence.ArtifactMain\"), so I promoted it. A gate test forbids verified entries pointing into `prebuilt/`, so it goes through a small new wrapper, `lib/meta/jar.py:main_class`, with a `_BUILTIN` entry for day 22. I removed the key from the prebuilt `FIELDS`. I added offline tests for the codec, the jar field and the web handlers (local servers, including a 410 target and a 3-target `solve()`) to `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`.\n5. **Rejected or not applicable:** the binary and scripting NOTES proposals (`lib.common` AES-unzip and `gm_error_body`/`iter_entries` helpers) are older solver plumbing, not today's GM-confirmed facts. Mobile, binary and scripting typed no new codec branch on day 22 (mobile uses only `lib.android`), so there was nothing to fold in.\n\nSeveral other files under `lib/` were already uncommitted when I started (`android.py`, `binary.py`, `codec.py`, `decode.py`, `vocab.json`, and new untracked files like `lib/meta/apk.py`). I left them alone. The files I edited were:\n- `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py`\n- `lib/web/__init__.py`\n- `lib/websolve.py`\n- `lib/warmups_codecs.py`\n- `lib/meta/__init__.py`\n- `lib/meta/jar.py` (new)\n- `lib/meta/prebuilt/jar.py`\n- `lib/knowledge.py`\n- `tests/test_day7_fixes.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1391,"cache_read_input_tokens":107019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1391},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e761320-118b-4e21-b38e-4dfe6997f088","uuid":"f56ebdf5-236a-451f-84d4-2e6ec7d11a66","timestamp":"2026-10-22T13:19:28.139Z","request_id":"req_011CgHLpLNzqaiPASMccd9wm"}
